{
  "uid": "tickwatch-instrumented",
  "title": "Instrumented",
  "description": "What are your own resources doing? Empty unless a resource calls the tickwatch export API — nothing here is collected automatically.",
  "tags": ["tickwatch"],
  "editable": false,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "15s",
  "time": { "from": "now-3h", "to": "now" },
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "tickwatch",
      "type": "dashboards",
      "tags": ["tickwatch"],
      "asDropdown": false,
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": true,
      "targetBlank": false,
      "icon": "external link"
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**This dashboard is empty until one of your resources calls the tickwatch export API.** Nothing on it is collected automatically — the exporter cannot see inside another resource, so database queries and events are pushed in by the code that performs them. See *Instrumenting your own resource* in the README.\n\nThe writes are cheap and they never raise: a rejected call is counted against `tickwatch_export_errors_total` and the calling resource carries on. If a panel here stays empty after you have added the calls, check that counter on the **Exporter** dashboard — it is where a wrong metric name goes."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Database queries by operation",
      "description": "Whatever the calling resource labels an operation — select, insert, update. Bounded by a series cap like everything else, so a caller passing the whole SQL string as the op label will hit the cap and be reported on the Exporter dashboard rather than quietly eating memory.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 4 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "tickwatch-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "tickwatch-prometheus" },
          "expr": "sum by (op) (rate(fivem_db_queries_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{op}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "decimals": 2,
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": { "mode": "normal", "group": "A" },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false
          },
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "text", "value": null }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Query latency p95 by operation",
      "description": "The dashed line is 50 ms, where DatabaseQuerySlow fires — and 50 ms is not a round number picked for looking sensible. It is one frame of this server's time budget, spent waiting on the database, on the main thread. A query at that latency is costing a whole frame.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 4 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "tickwatch-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "tickwatch-prometheus" },
          "expr": "fivem:db_query_duration_seconds:p95",
          "legendFormat": "{{op}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisSoftMax": 0.06,
            "thresholdsStyle": { "mode": "dashed" }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "transparent", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 0.05 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Query error ratio",
      "description": "Errors over total. The dashed line is 1%, where DatabaseErrorsRising fires.\n\nNOT YET RUN AGAINST DATA. This query has been parse-checked by promtool and never executed against a server with instrumented queries, because nothing has called the export API yet. Treat it as unproven until it has.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 13 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "tickwatch-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "tickwatch-prometheus" },
          "expr": "sum(rate(fivem_db_queries_total{status=\"error\"}[5m])) / sum(rate(fivem_db_queries_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "failing"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": false },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "single", "sort": "none" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 1,
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisSoftMax": 0.02,
            "thresholdsStyle": { "mode": "dashed" }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 0.01 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Events pushed, and how long they took",
      "description": "Event rate on the left axis, p95 duration on the right — two quantities that only make sense together. A slow event that fires once an hour is not a problem; a fast one firing a thousand times a second is.\n\nThe p95 series has NOT YET BEEN RUN against data, for the same reason as the error ratio above.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 13 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "tickwatch-prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "tickwatch-prometheus" },
          "expr": "sum by (event) (rate(fivem_events_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{event}} — rate"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "tickwatch-prometheus" },
          "expr": "fivem:event_duration_seconds:p95",
          "legendFormat": "{{event}} — p95"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false
          },
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "text", "value": null }] }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byFrameRefID", "options": "A" },
            "properties": [
              { "id": "unit", "value": "reqps" },
              { "id": "custom.axisLabel", "value": "events per second (left)" }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byFrameRefID", "options": "B" },
            "properties": [
              { "id": "unit", "value": "s" },
              { "id": "custom.axisPlacement", "value": "right" },
              { "id": "custom.axisLabel", "value": "p95 duration (right)" }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
